<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Sparkle is intentionally NOT configured for the Fire fork yet.
	  Setting SUFeedURL or SUPublicEDKey here would point at the upstream
	  jordanbaird/ice-releases appcast (the values that were here before)
	  or at a not-yet-existent fork appcast. Both routes risk Sparkle
	  proposing an "update" that silently moves users back to an upstream
	  build, undoing every fork-specific fix. Until a custom appcast is
	  hosted at pdurlej.github.io/fire-releases (ROADMAP Phase 0.3 follow-up,
	  blocked on generating a Sparkle EdDSA keypair via `brew install --cask
	  sparkle && sparkle/bin/generate_keys`), Sparkle stays disabled.

	  Users update by downloading a new DMG from
	  https://github.com/pdurlej/Ice/releases manually. The in-app
	  "Check for Updates" button will no-op (Sparkle returns an error
	  when SUFeedURL is missing).
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
